    "body": "## Summary\n- remove the redundant `topUpRequestId` from job-publication PaymentIntents\n- centralize publication PaymentIntent parameter construction for a testable contract\n- add regression coverage for amount, currency and the exact settlement metadata set\n\n## Rationale\nJob-publication settlement already keys on `purpose`, `jobPublicationId` and `userId`. Carrying a synthetic wallet top-up request identifier into Stripe was unnecessary and blurred the boundary between generic wallet funding and publication-scoped funding. This keeps provider metadata minimal while preserving all webhook reconciliation checks.\n\n## Validation\nCI and the dedicated job-publication payment smoke workflow are required before merge.",
